# Placeables — the build palette, as things you actually carry.
#
# ONE ITEM PER BUILDABLE BLOCK is the invariant here (see the `buildable` tag in
# content/blocks/*.block). It is what turns the old infinite material menu into
# an inventory: a slot you can run out of. The four commonest non-buildable digs
# (mud, ash, sticky, permafrost) get an item too, because a block you break a
# hundred times on the way down should not vanish into nothing.
#
# `places` is the whole behaviour. Everything else is presentation.

# --- Rock ------------------------------------------------------------------

@item gravel_pile
name      Gravel
category  placeable
color     138 130 118
icon      icon_block_cube
places    gravel
stack     99
value     1
desc      Loose enough to slump the moment it is unsupported.
tags      stone buildable

@item sandstone_block
name      Sandstone
category  placeable
color     200 175 120
icon      icon_block_cube
places    sandstone
stack     99
value     2
desc      Sand that has had a few million years to think about it.
tags      stone buildable
craft     in="sand_pile" n="4" out=1 station=workbench

